
<div class="exclude-fragments-input">
    <div class="form-group">
        <p>UniProt designates a Sequence Status for each member: Complete if the encoding DNA sequence has both start and
        stop codons; Fragment if the start and/or stop codon is missing. Approximately 10% of the entries in UniProt are
        fragments.</p>

        <div>
            <span class="input-heading">Exclude Fragments:</span>
            <span>
                {{ form_widget(form) }}
            </span>
        </div>
        
        <div class="input-description">
            <p>For the UniRef90 and UniRef50 databases, clusters are excluded if the cluster ID ("representative sequence") is a fragment.</p>
            <p>UniProt IDs in UniRef90 and UniRef50 clusters with complete cluster IDs are removed from the clusters if they are fragments.</p>
        </div>

        {{ form_errors(form) }}
    </div>
</div>

